# Quarkus worker development

- Use **OpenJDK 21** via `worker/mise.toml` (`openjdk-21.0.2`). Do not switch to Temurin for this project.
- Prefer `mise run dev|test|package|inject-metrics` from `worker/`. Those tasks source `scripts/podman-env.sh`.
- Kafka Dev Services: **Podman only**. Set `DOCKER_HOST` to the Podman API socket; never rely on Docker Desktop.
- Inject scripts discover Kafka with **podman** (`label=quarkus-dev-service-kafka`), not docker.
- JVM images: `registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9/openjdk-21*:1.24`. Allowed native micro: `quay.io/quarkus/ubi9-quarkus-micro-image:2.0`.
- Inference REST is sync: keep `@Blocking` on `@Incoming` Kafka consumers.
- Optional LLM: omit `INFERENCE_BASE_URL` to disable; never default it to empty string in config mappings.
- Inference is enrichment only (see `worker/README.md`); do not gate alert emission on LLM success.
- Local Ollama: `INFERENCE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1`, prefer `granite3.3:2b`; document cleanup with `ollama rm`.
